cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "holotype: forensic-grade archival of LLM-driven agent CLI sessions for scientific reproducibility"
message: "If you use this software in research that you publish, please cite the software as well as the deposited session bundles."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ferland
    given-names: Brenden
    affiliation: "Adamson Lab, University of Connecticut"
    email: brendenferland@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/PEEKPerformer/holotype"
url: "https://github.com/PEEKPerformer/holotype"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20349311"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.20349311"
    description: "Zenodo software DOI (v2.0.2)"
abstract: >-
  holotype is an agent-CLI-agnostic provenance tool that deposits LLM
  session transcripts (Claude Code, Codex, Google Antigravity, and
  user-defined sources) into a content-addressable, hash-chained git
  archive suitable for citation in scientific publications. Each
  deposited session is hashed (SHA-256), optionally compressed (zstd)
  and encrypted (git-crypt), and recorded in a manifest that captures
  per-session metadata (host CLI version, model identifiers, token
  totals, wall-clock duration, project-repo git state) needed for
  reproducibility. Bundled session subsets can be exported as
  Zenodo-ready deposits with stock-Unix-tool verification procedures
  (shasum, jq) for paper review independent of the holotype installation.
keywords:
  - "large language models"
  - "scientific reproducibility"
